{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 10, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "find 9x: 256 points, computing in u8, costs from gt1030\n  dot products under gt1030 (sums of products laid into lanes; cost 3 as written):\n  cost 2   u8(udot4x8(x, 9))\n           udot4x8 (4 x 8-bit lanes, unsigned): lane 0: x * 9\n           x in 0..255 (proved range)\n           udot4x8's sum is in 0..2295: it does not wrap\n           exhaustive\n  cost 2   x + (x << 3)                             exact\n  cost 3   9x                                       affine fit\n  cost 4   x + (x + 2 << 3) - 16                    affine fit\n  cost 5   3(x + (x + x))                           affine fit\n  cost 6   3(x + (x - 5 << 1)) + 30                 affine fit\n  [searched every term up to cost 4: 65536 distinct columns, bank full; 'more' continues]\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 10, "ok": true, "cmd": "find", "ucas": "find (x: u8)*3 3", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "find", "points": 256, "sampled": false, "type": "u8", "model": "gt1030", "peephole": [], "dot_products": {"model": "gt1030", "available": true, "cost_before": 3, "cost": 2, "expr": "u8(udot4x8(x, 9))", "relies_on": "udot4x8 (4 x 8-bit lanes, unsigned): lane 0: x * 9\nx in 0..255 (proved range)\nudot4x8's sum is in 0..2295: it does not wrap", "proof": "exhaustive"}, "implementations": [{"cost": 2, "expr": "x + (x << 3)", "why": "exact", "verified": true, "exhaustive": true, "proof": "exhaustive"}, {"cost": 3, "expr": "9x", "why": "affine fit", "verified": true, "exhaustive": true, "proof": "exhaustive"}, {"cost": 4, "expr": "x + (x + 2 << 3) - 16", "why": "affine fit", "verified": true, "exhaustive": true, "proof": "exhaustive"}, {"cost": 5, "expr": "3(x + (x + x))", "why": "affine fit", "verified": true, "exhaustive": true, "proof": "exhaustive"}, {"cost": 6, "expr": "3(x + (x - 5 << 1)) + 30", "why": "affine fit", "verified": true, "exhaustive": true, "proof": "exhaustive"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "find 9x: 256 points, computing in u8, costs from gt1030\n  dot products under gt1030 (sums of products laid into lanes; cost 3 as written):\n  cost 2   u8(udot4x8(x, 9))\n           udot4x8 (4 x 8-bit lanes, unsigned): lane 0: x * 9\n           x in 0..255 (proved range)\n           udot4x8's sum is in 0..2295: it does not wrap\n           exhaustive\n  cost 2   x + (x << 3)                             exact\n  cost 3   9x                                       affine fit\n  cost 4   x + (x + 2 << 3) - 16                    affine fit\n  cost 5   3(x + (x + x))                           affine fit\n  cost 6   3(x + (x - 5 << 1)) + 30                 affine fit\n  [searched every term up to cost 4: 65536 distinct columns, bank full; 'more' continues]\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 11, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: _eq0 has free variables: defined as _eq0(a, x, b)\n  note: _eq1 has free variables: defined as _eq1(x)\nfit _eq0 to _eq1 (max relative error, 257 sample points):\n  x = 0\n  b = 0.01220628624\n  objective 0.999878\n  0.01220628624\n  max abs error 99.9878 at x=-10\n  max rel error 29.5157 (2.95e+03%) at x=-0.02\n  mean rel error 1.05734 over 1001 points\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 11, "ok": true, "cmd": "fit", "ucas": "_eq0 = a*x + b\n_eq1 = x^2\nfit _eq0 ~ _eq1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "fit", "metric": "max relative", "sample_points": 257, "constants": [{"name": "x", "value": 0}, {"name": "b", "value": 0.012206286237409578}], "objective": 0.9998779371376258, "fitted": "0.01220628624", "max_abs_error": 99.98779371376258, "max_abs_at": "x=-10", "max_rel_error": 29.515715593525247, "max_rel_at": "x=-0.02", "mean_rel_error": 1.05733669179201, "points": 1001, "bad_points": 0}, "notes": [{"kind": "default", "text": "_eq0 has free variables: defined as _eq0(a, x, b)"}, {"kind": "default", "text": "_eq1 has free variables: defined as _eq1(x)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  note: _eq0 has free variables: defined as _eq0(a, x, b)\n  note: _eq1 has free variables: defined as _eq1(x)\nfit _eq0 to _eq1 (max relative error, 257 sample points):\n  x = 0\n  b = 0.01220628624\n  objective 0.999878\n  0.01220628624\n  max abs error 99.9878 at x=-10\n  max rel error 29.5157 (2.95e+03%) at x=-0.02\n  mean rel error 1.05734 over 1001 points\n"}, "isError": false}}
